{"sourceSha256": "083a9977ebe1b4a16329bf1fbcd603f6755491c57e16120637c5bcf23a6afd5b", "text": "Dear Dr Carter,\nRe: Mrs Jenny Perkins\n\n| am writing to réquest an urgent surgical assessment for Mrs Perkins, aged 65, who has\nfeatures suggestive of sigmoid volvulus following investigations.\n\nYesterday, Mrs Perkins visited the Emergency Department due to bilious vomiting and mild\nabdominal pain after having eaten a birthday cake a day before. Hence, she was treated for\n\nfood potsoning.\n\nToday, Mrs Perkins returned to the Emergency Department, complaining of worsening\nsymptoms associated with a decreased appetite and constipation. On physical examination,\n\nshe appeared lethargic and dizzy with clammy skin. Her abdomen was bloated and tender\non palpation. The bowel sounds were absent on auscultation. Her vital signs were not stable\nwith a BP of 90/60 mmhag and a pulse rate of 140 bpm. The investigation reports revealed\nlow levels of potassium, magnesium and creatinine with high a high level of urea in her\nblood. A coffee bean shaped mass was identified on an abdominal x-ray which indicates a\nlarge bowel obstruction. Therefore, she was commenced on IV fluids, analgesics and\n\nMrs Perkins has a history of Chron’s disease, moderate anorexia, and anhedonia. She has had\n\nvolvulus in her childhood as well. Her father died of colon cancer at the age of 64.\n\nYour ongoing surgical management would be highly appreciated. Should you have any\n\nqueries, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\nEmergency Doctor", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr Carter,\nRe: Mrs Jenny Perkins\n\n| am writing to réquest an urgent surgical assessment for Mrs Perkins, aged 65, who has\nfeatures suggestive of sigmoid volvulus following investigations.\n\nYesterday, Mrs Perkins visited the Emergency Department due to bilious vomiting and mild\nabdominal pain after having eaten a birthday cake a day before. Hence, she was treated for\n\nfood potsoning.\n\nToday, Mrs Perkins returned to the Emergency Department, complaining of worsening\nsymptoms associated with a decreased appetite and constipation. On physical examination,\n\nshe appeared lethargic and dizzy with clammy skin. Her abdomen was bloated and tender\non palpation. The bowel sounds were absent on auscultation. Her vital signs were not stable\nwith a BP of 90/60 mmhag and a pulse rate of 140 bpm. The investigation reports revealed\nlow levels of potassium, magnesium and creatinine with high a high level of urea in her\nblood. A coffee bean shaped mass was identified on an abdominal x-ray which indicates a\nlarge bowel obstruction. Therefore, she was commenced on IV fluids, analgesics and\n\nMrs Perkins has a history of Chron’s disease, moderate anorexia, and anhedonia. She has had\n\nvolvulus in her childhood as well. Her father died of colon cancer at the age of 64.\n\nYour ongoing surgical management would be highly appreciated. Should you have any\n\nqueries, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\nEmergency Doctor", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2314.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr Carter,\nRe: Mrs Jenny Perkins", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr Carter,", "x": 0.00864, "y": 0.00643, "width": 0.15601, "height": 0.02107, "confidence": 0.959, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.00864, "width": 0.15601, "confidence": 0.968}, {"text": "Dr", "x": 0.06612, "width": 0.02161, "confidence": 0.946}, {"text": "Carter,", "x": 0.0981, "width": 0.06655, "confidence": 0.961}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Mrs Jenny Perkins", "x": 0.00735, "y": 0.04821, "width": 0.22861, "height": 0.02107, "confidence": 0.951, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.00735, "width": 0.03328, "confidence": 0.941}, {"text": "Mrs", "x": 0.05186, "width": 0.03414, "confidence": 0.941}, {"text": "Jenny", "x": 0.09637, "width": 0.05575, "confidence": 0.968}, {"text": "Perkins", "x": 0.16076, "width": 0.07519, "confidence": 0.954}], "uncertainWords": []}]